{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Market Regime Detection Demo\n",
    "### Sequential Forward Filtering & Variance-Based State Alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates out-of-sample regime inference using a 2-state Gaussian Hidden Markov Model (HMM).\n",
    "\n",
    "* **State 0 (Calm / Low Volatility):** Steady trend dynamics, low conditional variance.\n",
    "* **State 1 (Turbulence / High Volatility):** Crisis or choppy conditions, high conditional variance.\n",
    "\n",
    "Probabilities are strictly computed via forward filtering \(P(S_t \\mid Y_{1:t})\) to guarantee **zero look-ahead bias**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.append(\"..\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.data_loader import fetch_sample_data, prepare_hmm_features\n",
    "from src.hmm_model import MarketRegimeHMM\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visual settings\n",
    "plt.style.use(\"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\" if \"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\" in plt.style.available else \"default\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Feature Engineering & Stationarity\n",
    "We load market bars and transform them into stationary 2D features: log returns and rolling volatility."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate reproducible regime-switching market data (800 daily bars)\n",
    "raw_df = fetch_sample_data(n_bars=800, seed=42)\n",
    "feature_df, X = prepare_hmm_features(raw_df, vol_window=21)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Feature matrix shape: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "feature_df.tail()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Fitting the Model with State Alignment\n",
    "The Baum-Welch (EM) algorithm fits the transition matrix and emission parameters. The model dynamically sorts states by total variance so State 0 is always the low-volatility state."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = MarketRegimeHMM(n_components=2, covariance_type=\"full\", random_state=42)\n",
    "model.fit(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Regime Transition Matrix (A):\")\n",
    "display(model.transition_matrix_)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Out-of-Sample Sequential Forward Filtering\n",
    "Computing regime probabilities strictly using information up to time \(t\)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "filtered_probs = model.predict_filtered_proba(X)\n",
    "regime_indices = model.predict_regimes(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_df[\"Regime\"] = regime_indices\n",
    "feature_df[\"Prob_LowVol\"] = filtered_probs[:, 0]\n",
    "feature_df[\"Prob_HighVol\"] = filtered_probs[:, 1]\n",
    "feature_df[\"Close\"] = raw_df.loc[feature_df.index, \"Close\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_df[[\"Close\", \"log_return\", \"volatility\", \"Regime\", \"Prob_HighVol\"]].tail()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Regime Visualizations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(14, 8), sharex=True, gridspec_kw={\"height_ratios\": [2.5, 1]})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subplot 1: Price colored by detected regimes\n",
    "dates = feature_df.index\n",
    "close_prices = feature_df[\"Close\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.plot(dates, close_prices, color=\"#1f2937\", lw=1.5, label=\"Asset Close Price\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Highlight High-Volatility Bear / Shock periods\n",
    "high_vol_mask = feature_df[\"Regime\"] == 1\n",
    "ax1.fill_between(dates, close_prices.min(), close_prices.max(), where=high_vol_mask,\n",
    "                 color=\"#ef4444\", alpha=0.25, label=\"Regime 1: High Volatility\")\n",
    "ax1.fill_between(dates, close_prices.min(), close_prices.max(), where=~high_vol_mask,\n",
    "                 color=\"#10b981\", alpha=0.10, label=\"Regime 0: Low Volatility / Calm\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.set_title(\"Market Regime Identification (Forward Filtered)\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(\"Price\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax1.legend(loc=\"upper left\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subplot 2: Filtered Probability of High Volatility State\n",
    "ax2.plot(dates, feature_df[\"Prob_HighVol\"], color=\"#dc2626\", lw=1.2, label=\"P(S_t = High Vol | Y_{1:t})\")\n",
    "ax2.axhline(0.5, color=\"#6b7280\", linestyle=\"--\", lw=1, label=\"Decision Threshold (0.5)\")\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(\"Probability\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel(\"Date\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylim(-0.05, 1.05)\n",
    "ax2.legend(loc=\"upper left\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
